 "name": "The Sally and the Muster Hall",
 "reading": "Giovanni's town is a garrison and its gym is the gate (data/gym_buildings/gym8.json: a gate mass with the walk on top of it, where he stands). Under the gate is what a garrison keeps beneath its gate: the bunker. A civil defender's command post, heavy and plain: you come down the gate's own newel stair into the sally, a long dark approach under four ranked bulkheads (the nth carries n orange rank marks), through a blast door into the muster hall, where the garrison falls in on orange marks painted on the floor. At the far end the shell gives out to the earth it was dug into: raw granite, coarse dirt and tuff in the walls, timber pit-props, and a doorway framed in spruce into the dug-out where the command dais stands with the situation map behind it. A ground type, in his own ground; and a defender, in the post that holds when the gate does not.",
